1
00:00:00,285 --> 00:00:02,142
Hi, we're NPC Union.

2
00:00:02,142 --> 00:00:04,085
I'm ZSYUYIIE.

3
00:00:04,085 --> 00:00:07,568
And I'm ChenHongshan333. We made this game in a

4
00:00:07,568 --> 00:00:10,456
forty-eight hour game jam, where the theme was Better

5
00:00:10,456 --> 00:00:11,738
Together.

6
00:00:11,738 --> 00:00:13,449
It's called Oh No My Hair.

7
00:00:13,449 --> 00:00:15,876
It's a puzzle platformer for two people sharing one

8
00:00:15,876 --> 00:00:18,986
keyboard, and neither of you can finish it alone.

9
00:00:20,264 --> 00:00:23,164
Two friends get to a salon right before closing,

10
00:00:23,164 --> 00:00:26,631
and the barber leaves his robot assistant in charge.

11
00:00:26,631 --> 00:00:28,670
The robot cuts way too much.

12
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:31,037
Their hair gets powers, the robot locks the front

13
00:00:31,037 --> 00:00:33,270
door, and the two of them have to find

14
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:34,159
another way out.

15
00:00:35,394 --> 00:00:37,325
Player one is Twin-Tails.

16
00:00:37,325 --> 00:00:39,825
She can glide and pull levers, and she can

17
00:00:39,825 --> 00:00:41,587
pick her friend up and fly with him.

18
00:00:42,839 --> 00:00:44,708
Player two is Pompadour.

19
00:00:44,708 --> 00:00:48,301
He dashes through hair gel, knocks flying scissors back,

20
00:00:48,301 --> 00:00:50,024
and can launch his friend off the top of

21
00:00:50,024 --> 00:00:51,332
his head.

22
00:00:51,332 --> 00:00:53,613
Every room is built around something one of them

23
00:00:53,613 --> 00:00:54,975
can't do on their own.

24
00:00:56,227 --> 00:00:58,060
This is our favourite move.

25
00:00:58,060 --> 00:01:01,664
Twin-Tails carries Pompadour over a pit, and he throws

26
00:01:01,664 --> 00:01:03,351
himself out of her grip.

27
00:01:03,351 --> 00:01:05,608
He smashes through a wall of gel that grows

28
00:01:05,608 --> 00:01:08,036
back, and she has to glide through the hole

29
00:01:08,036 --> 00:01:09,119
before it closes.

30
00:01:10,339 --> 00:01:12,682
The enemy's scissors end up helping you.

31
00:01:12,682 --> 00:01:15,788
Pompadour knocks one back, and Twin-Tails catches it in

32
00:01:15,788 --> 00:01:17,924
her pigtails and throws it straight up into a

33
00:01:17,924 --> 00:01:20,667
service bell. Ring the bell, and the next door

34
00:01:20,667 --> 00:01:21,338
opens.

35
00:01:22,573 --> 00:01:24,660
The salon gets in your way too.

36
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:27,184
Wet hair from the shampoo showers stops working, so

37
00:01:27,184 --> 00:01:31,413
Twin-Tails can't glide, and Pompadour bounces off the gel.

38
00:01:31,413 --> 00:01:33,585
A hair dryer fixes that, and its hot air

39
00:01:33,585 --> 00:01:34,438
lifts you up.

40
00:01:35,682 --> 00:01:38,267
At the end, you fight the assistant itself.

41
00:01:38,267 --> 00:01:41,094
It throws scissors, charges across the room, and calls

42
00:01:41,094 --> 00:01:42,986
in backup robots.

43
00:01:42,986 --> 00:01:44,952
You stun it with its own scissors, or by

44
00:01:44,952 --> 00:01:47,367
tricking it into a wall, then one of you

45
00:01:47,367 --> 00:01:48,739
lands on its head.

46
00:01:48,739 --> 00:01:51,178
Get hit, and it can swap your haircuts, so

47
00:01:51,178 --> 00:01:53,050
suddenly you have each other's powers.

48
00:01:54,330 --> 00:01:56,454
Both players have to matter in every room, so

49
00:01:56,454 --> 00:01:58,578
you end up shouting carry me, and wait for

50
00:01:58,578 --> 00:02:00,580
the water, at the person next to you.

51
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:01,979
That's our favourite part.

52
00:02:03,252 --> 00:02:06,346
It's for friends, siblings and couples who like puzzles.

53
00:02:06,346 --> 00:02:08,606
You only need one keyboard and a browser.

54
00:02:09,827 --> 00:02:13,128
There are already good co-op puzzle games Pico Park 2

55
00:02:13,128 --> 00:02:15,349
is built for groups of two to eight and

56
00:02:15,349 --> 00:02:18,380
ibb and obb is a two-player game about gravity

57
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:20,273
Ours is smaller and each of you has a

58
00:02:20,273 --> 00:02:22,749
power the other one doesn't We still have to

59
00:02:22,749 --> 00:02:24,633
find out whether people want that

60
00:02:25,906 --> 00:02:28,321
The prototype is finished and playable on itch dot

61
00:02:28,321 --> 00:02:31,197
io. Four chapters, twelve rooms, and a boss with

62
00:02:31,197 --> 00:02:33,215
three phases, with saved progress.

63
00:02:34,439 --> 00:02:36,733
To polish it and launch on Steam in twelve

64
00:02:36,733 --> 00:02:39,719
weeks, we need about seventeen thousand two hundred US

65
00:02:39,719 --> 00:02:41,024
dollars.

66
00:02:41,024 --> 00:02:43,208
Eight thousand eight hundred pays the two of us

67
00:02:43,208 --> 00:02:45,235
sixteen hundred a month each.

68
00:02:45,235 --> 00:02:48,172
That's the low end for small indie teams.

69
00:02:48,172 --> 00:02:51,570
Four thousand two hundred buys freelance art, music and

70
00:02:51,570 --> 00:02:52,872
sound.

71
00:02:52,872 --> 00:02:56,792
Thirteen hundred covers the Steam fee, playtests, tools, store

72
00:02:56,792 --> 00:02:58,508
art and a trailer.

73
00:02:58,508 --> 00:03:01,165
And the last twenty-nine hundred is a twenty percent

74
00:03:01,165 --> 00:03:01,739
buffer.

75
00:03:03,018 --> 00:03:05,251
If we raise nothing, we still ship a smaller

76
00:03:05,251 --> 00:03:07,375
version on about nine hundred dollars of our own

77
00:03:07,375 --> 00:03:08,762
savings.

78
00:03:08,762 --> 00:03:11,129
For the full version, we'd cover the production costs

79
00:03:11,129 --> 00:03:14,223
ourselves and run a small Kickstarter for our pay.

80
00:03:14,223 --> 00:03:16,338
Any prize money would be a bonus.

81
00:03:17,618 --> 00:03:19,778
Weeks one to four are playtests and fixing the

82
00:03:19,778 --> 00:03:22,545
tutorial. Weeks five to eight are polish, and the

83
00:03:22,545 --> 00:03:24,754
Steam page goes up by week eight.

84
00:03:24,754 --> 00:03:27,740
Weeks nine to twelve are accessibility, bug fixes, and

85
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:28,568
the release.

86
00:03:29,833 --> 00:03:33,171
Next we plan to test twenty player pairs tracking

87
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:37,246
unaided tutorial completion repeated failure points and willingness to

88
00:03:37,246 --> 00:03:41,596
play another room These are future validation targets not

89
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:43,283
achieved audience metrics

90
00:03:45,018 --> 00:03:46,936
That's us, NPC Union.

91
00:03:46,936 --> 00:03:50,455
We're looking for playtesters, feedback, and mentoring to get

92
00:03:50,455 --> 00:03:51,308
this finished.

93
00:03:52,550 --> 00:03:55,038
Scan the code, grab a friend, and give it

94
00:03:55,038 --> 00:03:56,229
a go.

95
00:03:56,229 --> 00:03:57,361
Thanks for watching!
